      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note: Having something that needs to be wrapped around the type part of a declaration (e.g. `Type value;`) is technically incorrect because it\u0027s not possible for all C types, e.g. `int (*x)[]` (pointer to array of int) which can\u0027t be separated into `int[]* x` or anything like that. (Clang nullability for this would look like `int (* _Nonnull x)[]`.)\n\nI think this problem is fine because it can be avoided using a typedef:\n```\ntypedef int intarray[];\nWGPU_NULLABLE(intarray *) x;\n```",
